# Code-is Basic — slice 3 lowerLocalCodes fixture
library "Code Is Basic".

// A single multi-layer library exercising `code is` local-source lowering end
// to end. Two `code is`-only concepts (lowered to a synthetic local codesystem
// + per-concept code in the Concepts layer, and a `[Resource: <code>]` retrieve
// in the Asserted layer) plus a `defined as` concept composing over them (the
// Inferred layer). The auto-split fans the lowered output across all three
// layers and re-qualifies the cross-layer refs. Because the synthetic
// terminology and its concept land in SEPARATE libraries here (Concepts vs
// Asserted), detectCollisions sees no same-library collision, so NO ` Code`
// suffix fires — the layered code names are bare "<X>" (the ` Code` suffix is
// a per-CRL-only artifact, where terminology + concept co-reside):
//   - the Asserted retrieves' code refs -> "Code Is Basic Concepts"."<X>"
//   - the Inferred composition's concept refs → "Code Is Basic Asserted"."<X>"

// ============ Locally-coded leaves (`code is`) ============

concept "Adult Patient":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `adult-18-or-older`.

concept "Active Crohns Disease":
- type is Condition.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `active-crohns-disease`.

// ============ Inferred (defined as over the coded leaves) ============

concept "Adult With Crohns":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as
(
   "Adult Patient"
   sem-and
   "Active Crohns Disease"
).
